/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/AsO4-formation.dat -- the first 3 dissociations of arsenic acid, written from the master:
      H3AsO4  <=>  AsO4 + 3 H+

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 2.31, dH1 = -7.8 kJ/mol
      pK2 = 7.05, dH2 = 1.7 kJ/mol
      pK3 = 11.9, dH3 = 15.9 kJ/mol
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  This record carries the sum of the first 3 steps (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
  dCp is not printed for arsenic acid.  The existing species H2AsO4 and HAsO4 carry NBS formation data (C320) and the new records are written from the neutral master H3AsO4.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species AsO4; masters ( { ion H3AsO4; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -3; } );
      logK25 -21.26; dH 9800; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 359, and Section 7.9, p. 248: pK1 2.31, dH1 -7.8 kJ/mol, pK2 7.05, dH2 1.7 kJ/mol, pK3 11.9, dH3 15.9 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
